The ONE change our custom firmware needs.

File to edit (inside the installed OpenCR Arduino board package -- path varies
by OS, see README.md "Where the library lives"):

    .../libraries/turtlebot3_ros2/src/turtlebot3/turtlebot3.cpp

Find the test-drive call (it sits near the LED/voltage diagnosis block, inside
the periodic update that TurtleBot3Core::run() drives) and comment it out:

--- turtlebot3.cpp   (stock)
+++ turtlebot3.cpp   (RobotKub: SW1/SW2 must not move the robot)
@@
   /* For diagnosis */
   // Show LED status
   diagnosis.showLedStatus(get_connection_state_with_ros2_node());
   // Update Voltage
   diagnosis.updateVoltageCheck(true);
-  // Check push button pressed for simple test drive
-  test_motors_with_buttons(diagnosis.getButtonPress(3000));
+  // RobotKub WRG2026: DISABLED. SW1/SW2 are mission buttons (start / e-stop /
+  // resume) handled in ROS (ttb3_mission/button_handler). The robot must not
+  // test-drive itself when a button is pressed.
+  // test_motors_with_buttons(diagnosis.getButtonPress(3000));

   /* For sensing and run buzzer */

That is the only edit. Do NOT touch update_gpios() -- it still reads SW1/SW2
into control_items.push_button[0]/[1], which is what gets published on
/sensor_state. Removing only the test_motors_with_buttons() call keeps button
REPORTING intact while removing the unwanted MOTION.

After editing, rebuild + upload the turtlebot3_burger_custom sketch (README.md).
